## 3. Conversion hierarchy (THE SPINE)

Order matters. Primary is what Smart Bidding optimizes toward. Secondary is "track but don't optimize."

| Stage | Type | Primary? | Value | Source |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| Lead form submission | Conversion | No (secondary) | $1 | Website + GTM |
| MQL | Offline upload | No | $25 | OCI sheet |
| SQL | Offline upload | No | $50 | OCI sheet |
| Opportunity | Offline upload | No | $500 | OCI sheet |
| Closed-Won | Offline upload | **YES** | ACV ($[ACV]) | OCI sheet |

- **OCI Google Sheet ID**: [SHEET ID — see `skills/oci-template-sheet/` for format]
- **Conversion window (primary action)**: **90 days** (B2B default; never less)
- **Attribution model**: Data-driven (or Position-based for low-volume)

## 4. Account structure (required archetypes)

Every B2B SaaS account should have these. Audit will flag missing ones.

- [ ] **Brand** — Exact + Phrase on company name + product names + permutations. Defensive.
- [ ] **Competitor** — Top 5 competitor brand names. Tight ad groups per competitor.
- [ ] **Non-brand product** — Category terms with commercial intent (e.g. "[product category] software", "[product category] platform").
- [ ] **Non-brand problem** — Pain-point queries (e.g. "reduce [pain]", "improve [outcome]").
- [ ] **Remarketing (RLSA)** — Audience layered on broader queries.

Optional:
- [ ] **DSA** — Dynamic Search Ads against the website, with controlled categories.
- [ ] **YouTube / Demand Gen** — Top-of-funnel only after Search is profitable.

## 5. Bidding rules

These are enforced by the audit and by the skills. Override per campaign with a documented reason.

- **Default bid strategy**: Maximize Conversions with Target CPA cap (cap = [TARGET_CAC] / [MQL→Closed-Won rate])
- **Volume floor for Smart Bidding**: 30 conversions / 30 days at the campaign level. Below floor → Maximize Clicks + Exact Match only.
- **Broad match prerequisite**: OCI must be flowing successfully for 30+ days, and the campaign must have a Target CPA / Target ROAS in place. Default = OFF.
- **Auto-applied recommendations**: **OFF**, all types.
- **Search Network expansion (Display)**: **OFF**.
- **Search partners**: **OFF** unless data proves otherwise.

